{"step_index":106,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T23:03:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T18:03:11-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T18:03:15-05:00\nThe search for \"\"GTA 6\" OR \"GTA VI\" mission walkthrough prerequisites \"unlocks\" OR \"requires\" Chapter 1 OR Chapter 2\" returned the following summary:\nIn ***Grand Theft Auto VI***, the campaign structure is divided into distinct chapters—primarily **Chapter 1 (Set in the Leonida Keys)** and **Chapter 2 (Set around Port Gellhorn and Kelly County)**—before moving toward Vice City[1][2][3]. Because GTA VI does **not** feature a mission replay menu or chapter select, tracking mission unlocks, prerequisites, and hard cutoffs between Chapter 1 and Chapter 2 is vital[1][4][3].\n\n---\n\n### **Chapter 1: \"Just Like Paradise\" (Leonida Keys)**\n* **Primary Focus:** Primarily introduces Jason and builds out the early smuggling and criminal web in the Keys[5][6]. \n* **Notable Mission Structure & Unlocks:**\n  * **Prologue:** Lucia’s introductory sequence[6].\n  * **Early Missions:** Operations like *Gone Fishing*, *Gear Up*, *Lab Fees*, and *Island Dreams* establish baseline cash flow and open up initial mechanics[6].\n  * **Key Unlocks:** \n    * Completing ***Island Dreams*** unlocks the initial **Kenton Sets** / strand activities[7].\n    * Side activities and optional tasks like *Get Shirley’s Rum*, *Skunk Apeology 101*, and text-based jobs from Cal become available during Chapter 1[8].\n* **Chapter 1 Cutoff / Transition Warning:** \n  * The final missions of Chapter 1 lead directly into a forced location shift. Certain activities, text triggers (such as specific lines from Cal), and ambient character moments must be completed before starting the chapter's final transition mission (often referenced as *Tourist Trap* or the final narrative bottleneck)[2][9]. \n  * *Tip:* Players frequently manual-save right before the end of Chapter 1 because you cannot replay missions later[4][3].\n\n---\n\n### **Chapter 2: \"Paradise Lost\" (Port Gellhorn / Kelly County)**\n* **Primary Focus:** Shifts focus heavily to Lucia as the duo lays low around Port Gellhorn, introducing survival mechanics, motel management, and new local contacts[10].\n* **Notable Mission Structure & Unlocks:**\n  * Begins with missions tracking the infamous bag (*What's in the Bag?*) and dealing with living expenses (*Overnight Charges*, *Just Moved In*)[10].\n  * **Key Unlocks & Prerequisites:**\n    * **Vehicle Fencing & Registration:** You unlock the ability to register your dream car and fence vehicles after completing the Chapter 2 main mission **Moses** (*Take a Vehicle to Moses*) and interacting with the Slim Jim mechanic[7][11].\n    * **Free Character Switching:** Starting with the Chapter 2 main mission **\"Coffee Break,\"** the game permanently unlocks the ability to freely switch back and forth between Jason and Lucia in the open world by holding right on the D-pad[1].\n    * **Business Ventures:** Port Gellhorn criminal operations and side ventures (such as *Kolt and Associates*) open up early in Chapter 2 for steady passive income[11].\n    * **Meditation / Collectibles:** Certain ambient world unlocks, like tracking down specific Meditation spots for the *Positive Mental Attitude* requirements, can be safely started or cleaned up here if missed during Chapter 1's tighter bottlenecks[12].\n\n---\n\n### **Core Gameplay Rules to Keep in Mind:**\n1. **No Mission Replay:** Just like *Red Dead Redemption 2*, once a mission from Chapter 1 or 2 is finished, it's locked to that playthrough save file[1][4]. \n2. **Missable Side Content:** Time-sensitive optional missions are marked with an hourglass icon; failing to tackle them before pushing the main narrative forward causes them to drop off the map[4]. \n3. **Manual Saves:** Always keep a master manual save file at the tail end of Chapter 1 and Chapter 2 if you intend to experience alternate choices without restarting the entire 60+ hour campaign[4][3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [clarin.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFluVnII8clIcAPp6sjMLrbGsKRN6pOF_7vg9CUCg_hFLlx-V1V5HycYUq5Z8P_QAeKQv8FzFzaqwuIpasZsVv4P3IgBX-p2_GsFTNGD28_2wNCXrPIGiTx0__smy8DHxhHmcfpRCeJsXe0UlPPSP3HrGUuA4YlAOST9pvt9NAmOJyX3WZdRQceEPG5K_6nMgkjS5deng_tEK2DIK7rA5qYckBKoZcCiJWxUfg=)\n[2] [gamesradar.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEopgqngxoyf4GKkHCOOoAhSw5WLubFV-gW90_DvPsAjOQMQu8jPMzbsId53to0VwAWosZ3e4aNtt5ZC--ZrTrLz4SFy8tfo-SMqIPj5hFs38uMTHEOGh71J5vmPefhtEegbZ8IzfP5IA7mqt4K8sdRjcathTi8VTbyEsw=)\n[3] [g2a.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHkjQu3OVp-qtvr1govtbygdwB-mbYiONJduapLLlaU0KD9F5GtClM0_3z2R_Ee8LlKP8sD0CeKkmak29H5z4MwsxwD1-WZ8hn_359ezCykHifdWkXh-_XpzZgWE3_BVMaCg4WDIbjyCUJQBCNLNoOViswfJjf9tnBS)\n[4] [powerpyx.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHzTtAdpPvQRqaBxAVSTR6SVXcLfhORTmKNhINU8iKELEekduoHQdwOT7CAVeRfrwiL_DJbDSRjdLULe_JOYVyX44bX5AnwVWTW1-RVwRU5XhgiRkxrmhJQQov7cO8vK26KWRs73RShSx4b8Gy53uUvrPEb)\n[5] [redbull.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFiY1nvBOKpblKyQ51VEIx2CNGZG0nwAxe0o1Fl_yZKoLXDReyc4S0cLMEpshkb02i0jjeXTL8eBDeHIy321yFKkZsNHejz0S1_RWID6Ba0mXW9i2PBFKN2d46RJzF6lxGcxzR55OILIpW9EWAvxuQ=)\n[6] [pcgamer.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGZzBzWmN___1BVx1hoxovbpujjdBdtw6RZpZutCbK5rrx8KIIM5eU2DL2f8QKOsj--7N-Bf4crwi-3pU9tUx9QqOI-81JE5nTl_c0P0q5BRzqN6fwd2g3HU5wTPxO6aChPxDUMqkj_G0nQ8phLqAwU5IP8ywtXaDU=)\n[7] [rockpapershotgun.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHMPnTzuc60Q_kM3y8H7-E17A-XR32AjD_kW4q3QBoRUGQ4y7DbcQfGddNOoVlc8v2sOV4be340xN-E8BJbx7pl7SSBDCkLak7g5sHzlY-ybP6L1Piiivbl0vV8hFuuzVIpzZIoT2yrquf3o-aZ0-6Cbg35)\n[8] [ign.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFAY8-wfOzicwi2lHT2lbbJB2tmtBGUAItLfC0xu-bc40Lhpf