{"step_index":111,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T23:03:28Z","thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe artifact path seems valid. The flowchart will be structured to detail the mission flow with Mermaid diagrams, ensuring valid syntax and quoted labels for special characters. The artifact will include an executive summary and then flowcharts for individual chapters with prerequisites and key elements.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive GTA VI Campaign Mission Flowchart and Prerequisite Matrix detailing chapter-by-chapter dependencies, unlock conditions, character switching milestones, heist preparation trees, points of no return, and finale endings.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Grand Theft Auto VI: Campaign Mission Flow & Prerequisite Guide\n\nThis document maps the mission dependency graph, prerequisite unlock trees, character-switching milestones, heist setup pipelines, and points of no return across the 5 story chapters of *Grand Theft Auto VI*.\n\n---\n\n## 1. High-Level Campaign Architecture\n\nThe GTA VI storyline progresses through five distinct geographical and thematic narrative blocks. While open-world exploration is available between operations, missions operate in a strict Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) with key narrative bottlenecks connecting each chapter.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph P[\"Prologue & Chapter 1\"]\n        C1[\"Just Like Paradise<br/>(Leonida Keys & Key Lento)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph C2B[\"Chapter 2\"]\n        C2[\"Paradise Lost<br/>(Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph C3B[\"Chapter 3\"]\n        C3[\"Tits, Ass, Drug Money<br/>(Vice City Outskirts & Metro Cartels)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph C4B[\"Chapter 4\"]\n        C4[\"Vice City, Baby<br/>(Vice City Metro & Ocean Beach)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph C5B[\"Chapter 5\"]\n        C5[\"Top of the World, Ma!<br/>(Climax & Resolution)\"]\n    end\n\n    C1 -->|\"Bottleneck: Discharge Time\"| C2\n    C2 -->|\"Bottleneck: Checking Out\"| C3\n    C3 -->|\"Bottleneck: Ocean Beach\"| C4\n    C4 -->|\"Point of No Return: Sunset\"| C5\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise (Leonida Keys)\n\n### Mechanics & Structure\n- **Playable Character**: Strictly locked to **Jason** (with Lucia introduced in the Prologue and reunited in *\"Coming Home\"*).\n- **Core Narrative**: Petty smuggling, local debt enforcement for Brian, and settling in Key Lento following Lucia's release from Hamlet State Penitentiary.\n- **Critical Milestone**: Completing *\"Island Dreams\"* opens local diving and strand activities; *\"Tourist Trap\"* begins the irreversible sequence into Chapter 2.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    M01[\"1. Prologue<br/>(Lucia Prison Interview)\"] --> M02[\"2. Gone Fishing<br/>(Jason & Donnie Smuggling)\"]\n    M02 --> M03[\"3. Gear Up<br/>(Brian's Armory)\"]\n    M03 --> M04[\"4. Just a Scratch<br/>(Ganado Repair)\"]\n    M04 --> M05[\"5. Lab Fees<br/>(Brian's Rent Collection)\"]\n    \n    M05 --> M06[\"6. Unwanted Attention<br/>(Cal's Hamlet Trip)\"]\n    M06 --> M07[\"7. Pipework<br/>(Marina Odd Jobs)\"]\n    M07 --> M08[\"8. Hey Arnold!<br/>(Broker Interrogation)\"]\n    M08 --> M09[\"9. Island Dreams<br/>(Keys Diving Unlocked)\"]\n    M09 --> M10[\"10. Feng Shui<br/>(Moving Furniture)\"]\n    \n    M10 --> M11[\"11. Coming Home<br/>(Lucia Released from Prison)\"]\n    \n    M11 --> M12[\"12. Clean Up After Donnie\"]\n    M12 --> M13[\"13. Buck Me<br/>(Banking App Setup)\"]\n    M13 --> M14[\"14. Down to Earth<br/>(Marina Drug Run)\"]\n    M14 --> M15[\"15. Clear Skies<br/>(Southwind Bikers)\"]\n    \n    M15 --> M16[\"16. Day Release<br/>(Rusty Anchor Night Out)\"]\n    M16 --> M17[\"17. Swamped<br/>(Kingfishers Smugglers)\"]\n    M17 --> M18[\"18. Don Gone<br/>(Clearing Donnie's Trailer)\"]\n    M18 --> M19[\"19. Recalibration<br/>(Cal Intervention)\"]\n    \n    M19 --> M20[\"20. Tourist Trap<br/>(Mattia's Offer - Transition Starts)\"]\n    M20 --> M21[\"21. Home Sweet Home<br/>(Key Lento Fallout)\"]\n    M21 --> M22[\"22. Discharge Time<br/>(Chapter 1 Climax)\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Chapter 2: Paradise Lost (Port Gellhorn)\n\n### Mechanics & Structure\n- **Playable Character**: Heavily centered on **Lucia** during early recovery, then **permanently unlocks Dual Character Switching** via *\"Coffee Break\"*.\n- **Vehicle Fencing**: Unlocked via *\"Moses\"* (enabling Slim Jim vehicle thefts and custom garage registrations).\n- **Narrative Bottleneck**: *\"Checking Out\"* concludes Port Gellhorn motel residency and moves operations to Vice City.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    C1_End[\"From Ch. 1: Discharge Time\"] --> M23[\"23. What's in the Bag?<br/>(Starlet Motel Arrival)\"]\n    M23 --> M24[\"24. Overnight Charges\"]\n    M24 --> M25[\"25. Take Care of Jason<br/>(Lucia Solo Medical Run)\"]\n    M25 --> M26[\"26. Just Moved In\"]\n    \n    M26 --> M27[\"27. Girls' Trip\"]\n    M27 --> M28[\"28. Moses<br/>(Vehicle Fencing Unlocked)\"]\n    M28 --> M29[\"29. New Look\"]\n    M29 --> M30[\"30. How Do I Look?\"]\n    M30 --> M31[\"31. Behind on Payments\"]\n    \n    M31 --> M32[\"32. Ambulance Chaser\"]\n    M32 --> M33[\"33. Painkiller Supplier\"]\n    M33 --> M34[\"34. Daily Driver\"]\n    M34 --> M35[\"35. Pick Up A Gun\"]\n    M35 --> M36[\"36. Slam Dunk\"]\n    M36 --> M37[\"37. Breakfast Run\"]\n    \n    M37 --> M38[\"38. Coffee Break<br/>★ UNLOCKS DUAL CHARACTER SWITCHING ★\"]\n    \n    M38 --> M39[\"39. Hit Avery Pawn<br/>(Robbery System Demo)\"]\n    M39 --> M40[\"40. Hit Kingpin Bowling\"]\n    M40 --> M41[\"41. Impounded Vehicle\"]\n    M41 --> M42[\"42. Afternoon Delight\"]\n    M42 --> M43[\"43. Prepare for Vice City\"]\n    M43 --> M44[\"44. Checking Out<br/>(Move to Vice City)\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Chapter 3: Tits, Ass, Drug Money (Vice City Infiltration)\n\n### Mechanics & Structure\n- **Scope**: Largest chapter in the game (26 main missions).\n- **Key Factions**: Boobie Ike, Raul Bautista, Colombian Cartel (*La Polilla Negra*).\n- **Major Heist**: **The Sinfrontera National Bank Heist**. The heist involves a mandatory scoping phase followed by 5 modular preparation/intel missions that govern the vault timer, police response speed, and final crew survival.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    C2_End[\"From Ch. 2: Checking Out\"] --> M45[\"45. Welcome to Vice City\"]\n    M45 --> M46[\"46. Dealer's Choice\"]\n    M46 --> M47[\"47. Meet the Heders\"]\n    M47 --> M48[\"48. Dubious Provenance\"]\n    M48 --> M49[\"49. Mami Knows Best\"]\n    M49 --> M50[\"50. South Leonida Real Estate\"]\n    \n    M50 --> M51[\"51. Tyrone\"]\n    M51 --> M52[\"52. Here, Kitty Kitty\"]\n    M52 --> M53[\"53. Car Service\"]\n    M53 --> M54[\"54. Top Billing\"]\n    M54 --> M55[\"55. Boobie Time\"]\n    M55 --> M56[\"56. First Impressions\"]\n    \n    M56 --> M57[\"57. Caught Slipping\"]\n    M57 --> M58[\"58. Crosstown Traffic\"]\n    M58 --> M59[\"59. Credit Check\"]\n    M59 --> M60[\"60. Steal the Zorrusso for Randy\"]\n    \n    subgraph Heist_Prep[\"Sinfrontera Bank Heist Pipeline\"]\n        M61[\"61. Sinfrontera National Bank<br/>(Heist Scope Out)\"]\n        \n        M61 --> P1[\"62. Security Expert<br/>(Retrieve Nicole Park)\"]\n        M61 --> P2[\"63. Company Property<br/>(Steal Vault Explosives)\"]\n        M61 --> P3[\"64. The Missing Link<br/>(Interrogate Monty)\"]\n        \n        P1 --> P4[\"65. Safe Word<br/>(Safe-Cracking Training)\"]\n        P2 --> P5[\"66. Hidden Charges<br/>(Rig 3 Cell Towers - Delays Police)\"]\n        \n        P3 --> P6[\"67. Ride or Die\"]\n        P4 --> P7[\"68. Cooties\"]\n        P5 --> P8[\"69. Bricked Up\"]\n        \n        P6 & P7 & P8 --> M70[\"70. The Cartel Heist<br/>(Sinfrontera Vault Score)\"]\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Chapter 4: Vice City, Baby (The Syndicate & The Airport)\n\n### Mechanics & Structure\n- **Scope**: 25 main missions.\n- **Safehouse**: Y Hotel (Ocean Beach).\n- **Prerequisite Gate**: Abe Gonzalez demands a $75,000 BuckMe transfer to advance past *\"Party Hard\"*.\n- **Major Heist**: **VCIA Takedown** (Vice City International Airport cargo raid).\n- **Point of No Return**: Completing *\"VCIA Takedown\"* opens the *\"Tie Up Loose Ends\"* roaming window. Triggering *\"Sunset\"* permanently locks the world into the Chapter 5 endgame state.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    C3_End[\"From Ch. 3: The Cartel Heist\"] --> M71[\"71. Ocean Beach<br/>(Y Hotel Safehouse)\"]\n    M71 --> M72[\"72. Another Life\"]\n    M72 --> M73[\"73. Company Cars\"]\n    M73 --> M74[\"74. Lawyer Up\"]\n    M74 --> M75[\"75. Party Hard<br/>($75k BuckMe Wire to Abe)\"]\n    \n    M75 --> M76[\"76. Heavy Lifting\"]\n    M76 --> M77[\"77. Photo/Shoot\"]\n    M77 --> M78[\"78. Making Gainz\"]\n    M78 --> M79[\"79. Watch It\"]\n    M79 --> M80[\"80. Cash Injections\"]\n    M80 --> M81[\"81. Amateur Hour\"]\n    M81 --> M82[\"82. Dirty Work\"]\n    M82 --> M83[\"83. Too Much Baggage\"]\n    \n    subgraph Airport_Heist[\"VCIA Takedown Pipeline\"]\n        M83 --> M84[\"84. Adventures in Babysitting\"]\n        M84 --> M85[\"85. Fresh Evidence\"]\n        M85 --> M86[\"86. Power Play\"]\n        M86 --> M87[\"87. Child's Play\"]\n        M87 --> M88[\"88. Headliners<br/>(Dre'Quan Climax)\"]\n        \n        M88 --> M89[\"89. Close Surveillance\"]\n        M89 --> M90[\"90. Delivery Method\"]\n        M90 --> M91[\"91. Team Building\"]\n        M91 --> M92[\"92. Fully Catered<br/>(Catering Van Smuggling)\"]\n        \n        M92 --> M93[\"93. VCIA Takedown<br/>(Major Airport Heist)\"]\n    end\n    \n    M93 --> M94[\"94. Sunset<br/>★ POINT OF NO RETURN ★\"]\n    M94 --> M95[\"95. Starting From Zero<br/>(Transition to Chapter 5)\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Chapter 5: Top of the World, Ma! (Climax & Endings)\n\n### Mechanics & Structure\n- **Scope**: 7 explosive main story missions.\n- **Major Tactical Raid**: *\"Operation Savage Glory\"* (Coast guard facility raid & bridge destruction with Giorgio Gallo).\n- **The Binary Finale Trigger**: *\"Protective Custody\"* requires meeting Abe Gonzalez. The player is presented with a strict prompt:\n  - **\"Postpone\"**: Exit and complete any remaining world exploration or bank $2,000,000 for savings thresholds.\n  - **\"Proceed\"**: Initiates a continuous ~60-minute non-stop combat and set-piece gauntlet culminating in *\"The End of the Road\"*.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    C4_End[\"From Ch. 4: Starting From Zero\"] --> M96[\"96. Bird in the Hand\"]\n    M96 --> M97[\"97. Taking Liberties\"]\n    M97 --> M98[\"98. VC Baby\"]\n    M98 --> M99[\"99. Doggie Bag\"]\n    \n    M99 --> M100[\"100. Operation Savage Glory<br/>(Coast Guard Base Assault & Bridge Demolition)\"]\n    \n    M100 --> M101[\"101. Protective Custody<br/>(Giorgio's Betrayal & Precinct Ambush)\"]\n    \n    subgraph Endgame_Gauntlet[\"Final Lockdown Gauntlet\"]\n        M101 -->|\"Proceed Prompt\"| M102[\"102. The End of the Road<br/>(Penthouse Assault & Keys Escape)\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Endings[\"Branching Resolutions\"]\n        M102 --> E1[\"Ending A: Bonnie & Clyde<br/>(Requires 'Hot Together' Status + $2M Banked)\"]\n        M102 --> E2[\"Ending B: The Deal<br/>(Accept Mendez's Immunity Plea)\"]\n        M102 --> E3[\"Ending C: The Sacrifice<br/>(Solo Extraction Fallback)\"]\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Prerequisite & Unlock Reference Matrix\n\n| Chapter | Mission Name | Mandatory Prerequisite | Unlocked Feature / Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Ch. 1** | **Prologue** | Starting Game | Story start; Lucia introduction |\n| **Ch. 1** | **Gone Fishing** | Prologue | Introduces Jason; petty smuggling |\n| **Ch. 1** | **Island Dreams** | Hey Arnold! | Unlocks Kenton Sets & ocean diving |\n| **Ch. 1** | **Coming Home** | Feng Shui | Lucia released from Hamlet Penitentiary |\n| **Ch. 1** | **Tourist Trap** | Recalibration | Initiates Chapter 1 finale sequence |\n| **Ch. 1** | **Discharge Time** | Home Sweet Home | Hard transition to Port Gellhorn (Chapter 2) |\n| **Ch. 2** | **Moses** | Girls' Trip | Unlocks vehicle fencing & custom car registrations |\n| **Ch. 2** | **Coffee Break** | Breakfast Run | **Permanently unlocks dual-character switching** |\n| **Ch. 2** | **Hit Avery Pawn** | Coffee Break | Unlocks store/business stickup mechanics |\n| **Ch. 2** | **Checking Out** | Prepare for Vice City | Hard transition to Vice City (Chapter 3) |\n| **Ch. 3** | **Sinfrontera National Bank** | Steal the Zorrusso for Randy | Unlocks Bank Heist prep board |\n| **Ch. 3** | **Hidden Charges** | Company Property | Delays police response time in Cartel Heist |\n| **Ch. 3** | **The Cartel Heist** | All 5 Heist Preps completed | $10.5M max cartel take; transitions to Ch. 4 |\n| **Ch. 4** | **Party Hard** | Lawyer Up | Triggers $75,000 wire requirement to Abe |\n| **Ch. 4** | **Headliners** | Child's Play | Concludes Dre'Quan arc; unlocks airport recon |\n| **Ch. 4** | **VCIA Takedown** | Fully Catered | Completes major airport heist; rewards *Hi-Jacked* trophy |\n| **Ch. 4** | **Sunset** | VCIA Takedown | **Point of No Return** before Chapter 5 |\n| **Ch. 5** | **Operation Savage Glory** | Doggie Bag | Clears Leonida state heat; rewards *Snow Storm* trophy |\n| **Ch. 5** | **Protective Custody** | Operation Savage Glory | \"Proceed vs. Postpone\" decision point |\n| **Ch. 5** | **The End of the Road** | Protective Custody (Proceed) | Final campaign mission; triggers branching endings |\n","Description":"Complete GTA VI campaign mission flowchart, prerequisite tree, unlock milestones, and ending paths formatted with Mermaid diagrams and reference matrix.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\<user>\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\\gta6_mission_flow_chart.md","toolAction":"Writing mission flowchart artifact","toolSummary":"Create GTA 6 mission flowchart artifact"}}]}
