{"step_index":127,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T23:20:33Z","thinking":"Matplotlib with `tkagg` appears functional, allowing PNG file saving with specified DPI and tight bounding box. A Python script will be constructed to generate six PNG files, each representing a chapter with the filename `flowchart_chapter_X.png`.\n\n\nConsidering a multi-column snake layout or hierarchical grid for each chapter's nodes to ensure readability, visualizing the missions within each chapter. Chapter 1 will use a 4-column structure. Each column will contain a subset of missions, with arrows connecting the columns. This layout allows ample vertical and horizontal spacing. This pattern will be replicated for the missions in subsequent chapters like Chapter 2 and Chapter 3.\n\n\nChapter 4 structure identified: four columns for 25 missions, with a clear branching point leading to a \"point of no return\". Chapter 5's hierarchy includes a linear top sequence, a central mission, a trigger point, and a climax, leading to branching endings. A combined chart is envisioned, organizing all five chapters side-by-side with transition corridors.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Python script to render all 5 individual GTA VI chapter flowcharts and 1 master combined flowchart into high-resolution dark-mode PNGs.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.patches as patches\nimport os\nimport shutil\n\n# Styling Constants\nBG_COLOR = \"#0b0e14\"\nTEXT_COLOR = \"#ffffff\"\nSUBTEXT_COLOR = \"#9ca3af\"\n\n# Card Types & Colors\nSTYLES = {\n    \"normal\": {\n        \"bg\": \"#151922\",\n        \"border\": \"#22d3ee\",       # Cyan\n        \"title\": \"#38bdf8\",\n        \"badge_bg\": \"#083344\",\n        \"badge_fg\": \"#38bdf8\"\n    },\n    \"milestone\": {\n        \"bg\": \"#1c1427\",\n        \"border\": \"#f43f5e\",       # Rose / Neon Pink\n        \"title\": \"#fb7185\",\n        \"badge_bg\": \"#4c0519\",\n        \"badge_fg\": \"#f43f5e\"\n    },\n    \"heist\": {\n        \"bg\": \"#211a12\",\n        \"border\": \"#fbbf24\",       # Amber / Gold\n        \"title\": \"#fde047\",\n        \"badge_bg\": \"#451a03\",\n        \"badge_fg\": \"#fbbf24\"\n    },\n    \"point_of_no_return\": {\n        \"bg\": \"#280d16\",\n        \"border\": \"#ef4444\",       # Crimson\n        \"title\": \"#fca5a5\",\n        \"badge_bg\": \"#7f1d1d\",\n        \"badge_fg\": \"#fca5a5\"\n    },\n    \"ending\": {\n        \"bg\": \"#0c221a\",\n        \"border\": \"#10b981\",       # Emerald\n        \"title\": \"#34d399\",\n        \"badge_bg\": \"#064e3b\",\n        \"badge_fg\": \"#34d399\"\n    }\n}\n\ndef draw_card(ax, x, y, w, h, title, subtitle=\"\", badge=\"\", card_type=\"normal\", fontsize=9):\n    st = STYLES.get(card_type, STYLES[\"normal\"])\n    \n    # Outer box\n    rect = patches.FancyBboxPatch(\n        (x, y), w, h,\n        boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.03,rounding_size=0.15\",\n        linewidth=1.5,\n        edgecolor=st[\"border\"],\n        facecolor=st[\"bg\"],\n        zorder=3\n    )\n    ax.add_patch(rect)\n    \n    # Badge (if any)\n    if badge:\n        bx = x + w - 0.1\n        by = y + h - 0.08\n        ax.text(\n            x + w/2, y + h - 0.15,\n            badge.upper(),\n            ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n            fontsize=fontsize - 2.5,\n            fontweight=\"bold\",\n            color=st[\"badge_fg\"],\n            bbox=dict(boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.2\", facecolor=st[\"badge_bg\"], edgecolor=st[\"border\"], lw=0.8),\n            zorder=4\n        )\n        title_y = y + h/2 + 0.02\n        sub_y = y + 0.22\n    else:\n        title_y = y + h/2 + 0.12 if subtitle else y + h/2\n        sub_y = y + h/2 - 0.22\n\n    # Title\n    ax.text(\n        x + w/2, title_y,\n        title,\n        ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n        fontsize=fontsize,\n        fontweight=\"bold\",\n        color=st[\"title\"],\n        zorder=4\n    )\n    \n    # Subtitle\n    if subtitle:\n        ax.text(\n            x + w/2, sub_y,\n            subtitle,\n            ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n            fontsize=fontsize - 2,\n            color=SUBTEXT_COLOR,\n            zorder=4\n        )\n\ndef draw_arrow(ax, p1, p2, color=\"#38bdf8\", lw=1.6, rad=0.0):\n    connectionstyle = f\"arc3,rad={rad}\" if rad != 0 else \"arc3,rad=0\"\n    ax.annotate(\n        \"\",\n        xy=p2, xytext=p1,\n        arrowprops=dict(\n            arrowstyle=\"->,head_width=0.35,head_length=0.45\",\n            color=color,\n            lw=lw,\n            shrinkA=4,\n            shrinkB=4,\n            connectionstyle=connectionstyle\n        ),\n        zorder=2\n    )\n\nprint(\"Helper definitions loaded.\")\n","Description":"Helper functions for rendering flowcharts with Matplotlib","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\<user>\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\\scratch\\flowchart_helpers.py","toolAction":"Writing flowchart helpers","toolSummary":"Create flowchart helper script"}}]}
